A||||5||lennyb4||Please explain seat covers...||||1||
Z||000000||lennyb4||06-20-2000||08:26 AM||||I noticed people on here are always refering to seat covers. My seats are in horrible condition, i've tried aftermarket covers but they dont last very long. Im kinda confused on this issue. Does the factory covers just slip off & on or something? If not how hard are they to replace?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Helppppppp....||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-20-2000||09:13 AM||||We aren't generally talking about the $40 slip on seat covers from Wally World.  The seats have covers that can be removed.  I've never done it myself, but supposedly it only takes about an hour each.  The only problem I see is the cost of new seat covers.  I'm not sure you can find any for less than about $350/pr.  That's expensive!  I'd love to do some new seat covers, but I think I can get some different seats from a GM cousin for a lot less.  I was thinking about a set from a 3rd or 4th generation TA/Z28.  <A HREF="http://www.FIEROPROJECT.com" TARGET=_blank>www.FIEROPROJECT.com</A>  has a short article about using 3rd gen seats.  Pretty enticing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-20-2000||10:16 AM||||The factory seat covers can be removed. They are held in by "hogrings" You can replace them with stock looking covers for about $350 or you can go with leather for $400 and up. To do the swapping of covers takes about 1 hour per seat. You can also swap covers. So if somewhere you find a passenger seat in VGC you can remove the cover and recover the driverside seat. The bottoms can be swapped but you end up with a hole that cannot be seen. (it ends up between seat and console)||||reg||6
Z||000003||lennyb4||06-20-2000||10:25 AM||||Thanks guys.. I understand now. My bro-in-law has a 92 Berretta GTZ that the motor is on its last leg, BUT the seats are beautiful. I was thinking about doing a seat (and maybe brake) swap using his parts this winter ( or sooner if it finally dies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ). I do know the swap can be done but it will place the drivers haed approx. 1.5 to 2" closer to the top (and thats using the original fiero tracks) But only being 5"8" i could easily live with that.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-20-2000||12:33 PM||||Can't do the brakes without some serious fabrication.  They went to 10.25" discs in either '90 or '91.  If you decide not to use the seats, send 'em my way.  If they're the style I'm thinking of, I'd love to have them in my car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Big bolsters.  Almost reminds you of a racing seat?  Post a pic, please.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lennyb4||06-20-2000||01:17 PM||||Well forget the brakes then. And yep thats them alright. Big bolsters, adjustable lumbar, and the shade of gray is a really close match to what i have now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It will be awhile until i get them in (depends on how soon his car dies, but around fall at the latest) but i will post pics of all my mods as i complete them.||||reg||1
